<onlyinclude>'''Wafer testing''' is electrical characterization and screening of semiconductor devices while they remain on a wafer, before singulation and packaging. It includes process-monitoring measurements on test structures and product-die wafer sort; these have different sampling and disposition objectives.</onlyinclude>

== Scope ==
Wafer acceptance or parametric tests measure process-sensitive quantities such as transistor threshold voltage, leakage and sheet resistance, commonly on dedicated structures. Wafer sort uses a prober, probe card and automatic test equipment (ATE) to exercise individual product dies and assign test bins. A wafer map preserves spatial disposition for assembly and yield analysis. Passing wafer sort does not guarantee passing packaged final test or field reliability.

